and that you will not do another thing

267
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:40,960
until you have opened your journal

268
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:43,960
and written at least one page.

269
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:46,960
Otherwise, to be perfectly honest,

270
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:48,960
you might as well stop the tape now

271
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:51,960
and give it and the journal to a friend.

272
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:53,460
For surely if you lack

273
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:54,960
the discipline to start a journal,

274
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:56,960
it is highly unlikely that

275
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:58,960
you will ever have the discipline

276
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,960
to continue to use one either.

277
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:03,960
This leads us into a second function of your journal,

278
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:06,960
which is the capturing of good ideas.

279
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:09,960
How many times as we go through the day

280
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:11,960
do we come across a good idea,

281
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:13,960
a unique quote,

282
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,960
an interesting piece of information,

283
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:18,960
or even a significant personal discovery?

284
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:20,960
And each time we do,

285
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:22,960
we mentally say to ourselves,

286
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:24,960
I must remember that.

287
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:27,960
Now, I'm willing to admit here that the human mind,

288
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:30,960
I remember one time attending a church service

289
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:31,960
in Carmel,

290
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:32,960
and I was there.

291
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:35,960
I was there for a service in Carmel, California.

292
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:37,960
The sermon that Sunday morning was excellent,

293
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:40,960
so I opened my journal and started taking notes.

294
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:43,960
But out of the 400 people in attendance that day,

295
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:46,960
guess how many of the others were taking notes?

296
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:49,960
Not one.

297
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:51,460
So there I was taking notes

298
00:13:51,460 --> 00:13:52,960
in my journal from this sermon,

299
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:54,960
and pretty soon the people around me

300
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:57,960
were starting to give me strange looks.

301
00:13:57,960 --> 00:13:59,960
Out of the corner of my eye,

302
00:13:59,960 --> 00:14:01,960
I could see them nudging one another and whispering.

303
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:04,960
I felt like some kind of spy.

304
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:06,960
I could almost hear them saying,

305
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,460
he's going to get out of

306
00:14:08,460 --> 00:14:09,960
here with some of this stuff.

307
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:11,960
And sure enough, I did.

308
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:13,960
I got the stuff.

309
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:18,960
So what I'm suggesting is that you get in there

310
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:21,960
and get out with some of the stuff.

311
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:23,460
Let other people sit there

312
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:24,960
thinking they can remember it all.

313
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:27,960
Let other people treat opportunity casually,

314
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,960
but not you.

315
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:31,960
I would ask you to treat it that way.

316
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:33,960
Treat it seriously.

317
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:35,960
Let other people wonder at the end of their lives

318
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:38,960
where it all went wrong, but not you.

319
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:41,960
Let other people play while you work,

320
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:44,960
fool around while you study,

321
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:47,960
soak up the sun while you soak up ideas.

322
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:49,960
Ten years from now,

323
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:51,460
they'll still be trying to figure

324
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:52,960
out how to pay the bills,

325
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:56,960
or wondering why their marriage isn't working out,

326
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:59,960
or why they don't seem to be getting ahead professionally,

327
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:00,960
but not you.

328
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:07,960
Life always rewards the serious students for their labors.

329
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:10,960
So, since we all know that it's nearly impossible

330
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:13,460
for most of us to remember

331
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:15,960
the exact phrasing of an inspiring line

332
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:18,960
or the specific details of a business conference

333
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,960
over an extended period of time,

334
00:15:20,960 --> 00:15:25,960
we've got to get serious about capturing it now.

335
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,960
Generally, if we wait until the end of the day

336
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:31,960
to describe events and happenings and conversations,

337
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:35,960
the specific details have already escaped us.

338
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:39,960
At best, we are left with scattered fragments,

339
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:42,960
and it's hard to build an exciting future

340
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:46,960
from mere bits and pieces of the past and present.

341
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:49,460
So I would encourage you to get

342
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:51,960
it all down as it comes your way.

343
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:54,960
Financial ideas, personal development ideas,

344
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:59,960
time management ideas, family ideas, business ideas.

345
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,960
Everything you have to know

346
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:04,960
is what you have the good fortune to come across.

347
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:08,960
If an idea is worth listening to, worth reading,

348
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:10,960
worth remembering,

349
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:15,960
then it is also worth capturing in your journal.

350
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:17,960
And there are many reasons for

351
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:19,960
making the effort to capture good ideas,

352
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:22,960
not the least of which is the fact

353
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:25,960
that the simple act of writing something on paper

354
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:27,960
helps to etch the idea

355
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:29,960
more firmly in our conscious minds.

356
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:31,460
To hear it or see it

357
00:16:31,460 --> 00:16:32,960
or read it is one thing.

358
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,960
To take the time and make

359
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:36,960
the mental effort to capture it

360
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:41,960
with paper and pen is so much more.

361
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:45,960
Second, every idea has its time and place.

362
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:48,960
As Victor Hugo once wrote,

363
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:50,960
there is one thing stronger than

364
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:52,960
all the armies in the world,

365
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:57,960
and that is an idea whose time has come.

366
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:59,960
Perhaps the ideas you capture today

367
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:02,460
will not have any specific meaning or

368
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:04,960
purpose in your life at this moment,

369
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:07,460
but ultimately at some future point

370
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:09,960
in time when you march into battle,

371
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:12,960
the armory of ideas you have

372
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:15,960
carefully and conscientiously assembled over the years

373
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:18,960
will serve you well.

374
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:22,960
Here's another interesting phenomenon about ideas.

375
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:24,960
As we collect a variety of

376
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,960
thoughts on any given theme or subject,

377
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:29,460
there is a tendency for

378
00:17:29,460 --> 00:17:31,960
these individual ideas to come together

379
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:35,960
and form themselves into a whole new idea,

380
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:39,960
much as the single flakes of snow when gathered together

381
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:44,960
can be formed into snowballs and snowballs into snowmen.

382
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:46,960
Or perhaps a more graphic example

383
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:48,960
would be that of the igloo,

384
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:51,460
which is, after all, a

385
00:17:51,460 --> 00:17:53,960
dwelling built entirely of tiny snowflakes

386
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:55,960
which have been compressed by their weight

387
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:58,960
and frozen together over a period of time,

388
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:01,960
such that whole blocks of them may

389
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:04,960
be cut out to build a structure.

390
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:07,460
The successful human being is one

391
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:09,960
who has learned to diversify his interests

392
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:12,960
and gather knowledge from a variety of sources.

393
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:16,960
Gather enough good ideas in one area of life,

394
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:18,960
and you will form a solid block.

395
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:21,960
Gather enough solid blocks together,

396
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:24,960
and you can construct a whole new life.

397
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:28,960
But be aware of one thing.

398
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:30,460
The mental storage bank of

399
00:18:30,460 --> 00:18:31,960
good ideas is very much like

400
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:34,460
the bottom drawer of our desks

401
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:36,960
or the extra drawer in the kitchen

402
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:38,460
that holds a collection of

403
00:18:38,460 --> 00:18:39,960
valuable items gathered over the years,

404
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:42,460
none of which can ever be found

405
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:44,960
when we go to look for them again

406
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:48,960
because of the chaotic manner in which they were stored.

407
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:51,960
We pour information into our mental computers

408
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:53,960
much like we dump old letters

409
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:55,960
and store coupons into the extra drawer.

410
00:18:55,960 --> 00:19:00,960
Helter-skelter and hence, irretrievable.

411
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:02,960
One of the first things we attend

412
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:04,960
to when setting up a new business

413
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:08,960
is the development of a filing system for records

414
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:12,960
so that we can easily locate information whenever needed.

415
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,960
When we move into a new home,

416
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:16,960
we carefully pack all of

417
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,960
our possessions in clearly labeled boxes

418
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:20,960
so that we can find something

419
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:22,960
again in a hurry if needed.

420
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:24,960
But when it comes to facts,

421
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:25,960
to ideas,

422
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:26,960
to observations,

423
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:28,960
we have no system

424
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:30,960
as though they are incidental

425
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:33,960
rather than essential to our better future.

426
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:36,460
Your journal then provides you

427
00:19:36,460 --> 00:19:38,960
with the means of logically assembling

428
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:42,960
and storing the pieces of information that come your way.

429
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:45,960
Now there are many ways to assemble

430
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:48,960
the data in your journal for easy reference.

431
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:49,960
For example,

432
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:51,960
you might find it helpful to keep

433
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:53,960
an index at the back of each volume

434
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:56,960
so that you merely list the highlights of your entries

435
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:59,960
so that your index might read like this

436
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:06,960
Financial Ideas, pages 5, 53, 96, and 104

437
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:07,960
or

438
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:12,460
Ideas for Increasing Company Efficiency,

439
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:16,960
pages 46, 82, and 111.

440
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:19,960
At one time, I used to keep three journals

441
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:21,960
one for personal observations,

442
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:22,960
one for business notations,

443
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:25,960
and a third for creative ideas

444
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:28,960
for a book I was writing.

445
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:30,460
Of course, it didn't take

446
00:20:30,460 --> 00:20:31,960
me long to discard that system.

447
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:35,960
Carrying three journals around the world is no easy task.

448
00:20:35,960 --> 00:20:38,460
Then I tried using three colors

449
00:20:38,460 --> 00:20:40,960
of ink in the same journal

450
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:42,960
so that at a glance I could

451
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:44,960
focus on any one of the three areas.

452
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:47,460
While it was certainly easier

453
00:20:47,460 --> 00:20:49,960
carrying three pens than three journals,

454
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:52,960
it was still somewhat of a cumbersome system.

455
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:55,960
When the ideas are flowing fast and furious,

456
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:58,960
you don't always have the time to search

457
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:01,960
for a red, a green, or a blue pen.

458
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:03,960
The method I finally settled on

459
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:06,460
was setting aside certain sections

460
00:21:06,460 --> 00:21:08,960
of my journal for specific uses.

461
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:10,960
For example,

462
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:13,460
at the back of my journals I

463
00:21:13,460 --> 00:21:15,960
have a separate section for recording my goals,

464
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:18,960
for listing interesting quotes,

465
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:21,960
and for thoughts on new speech material.

466
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:23,460
Perhaps you may want to

467
00:21:23,460 --> 00:21:24,960
set aside part of your journal

468
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:27,960
for specific ongoing projects

469
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:29,960
or interests that you feel might

470
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,960
warrant a section of their own.

471
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:34,960
Choose one of these methods or devise a new one,

472
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:38,960
but make sure you set up some kind of system.

473
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:41,960
Remember, failure more often than not

474
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:45,960
is attributable to lack of information about how to succeed.

475
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:47,960
Each of us has the capacity

476
00:21:47,960 --> 00:21:49,960
to seek out the information we require

477
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:51,960
to achieve our goals.

478
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:53,960
Unfortunately,

479
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:56,460
we do not all have the

480
00:21:56,460 --> 00:21:58,960
discipline required to gather the data systematically

481
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:02,960
so that the raw material is easily accessible

482
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:05,960
and ready to be put into practical use

483
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:08,960
the moment opportunity presents itself.

484
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:10,960
How sad it would be if

485
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,960
opportunity came knocking on your door,

486
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:15,960
but you had to keep him waiting while

487
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:18,960
you rummaged through drawers and files for the key.

488
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:19,960
Undoubtedly,

489
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:20,960
by the time most people come in,

490
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:23,960
by the time most people have finally located the key,

491
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:27,960
opportunity has long since become impatient

492
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:29,960
and gone on to knock

493
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:31,960
on the door of someone else.

494
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:33,960
Next,

495
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:35,960
by taking the time to capture

496
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:37,960
and assemble information in our journals,

497
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:40,960
we now have the added benefit of being

498
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:43,960
able to review these ideas whenever we wish.

499
00:22:43,960 --> 00:22:46,460
You don't have to run back to the

500
00:22:46,460 --> 00:22:48,960
library to re-read the book you borrowed last year

501
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:51,960
or call a friend on the phone and

502
00:22:51,960 --> 00:22:54,960
try to reconstruct the conversation you had last month.

503
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:57,960
If you've captured the essence of the conversation

504
00:22:57,960 --> 00:23:00,960
or the highlights of the book in your journal,

505
00:23:00,960 --> 00:23:04,960
it will always be there for you to refer to.

506
00:23:04,960 --> 00:23:06,960
And here is the key point.

507
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:08,960
For your journals to have their greatest value,

508
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:11,960
they must be frequently reviewed.

509
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:13,960
You see, writing in journals is

510
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:15,960
merely a way of capturing information,

511
00:23:15,960 --> 00:23:17,960
but it is by re-reading our journals

512
00:23:17,960 --> 00:23:20,460
that we begin the process

513
00:23:20,460 --> 00:23:22,960
of translating information into practical knowledge

514
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:23,960
about ourselves,

515
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:25,960
our environment,

516
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:26,960
our relationships,

517
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:27,960
our businesses,

518
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:28,960
our financial affairs,

519
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:29,960
our dreams,

520
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:31,960
and our own better future.

521
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:34,460
I would strongly urge you to

522
00:23:34,460 --> 00:23:35,960
set aside a day each week,

523
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:37,960
or at the very least each month,

524
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:39,960
to review your recent entries.

525
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:41,960
And then once a year,

526
00:23:41,960 --> 00:23:43,960
take all of your journals off the shelf

527
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:45,960
and read them from cover to cover.

528
00:23:45,960 --> 00:23:47,960
What you read will provide you

529
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:50,460
with a story that will probably

530
00:23:50,460 --> 00:23:52,960
make an incredible story of personal growth.

531
00:23:52,960 --> 00:23:54,960
You see, more than anything else,

532
00:23:54,960 --> 00:23:56,960
a journal is a place to

533
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:58,960
document the development of your own life.

534
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:03,960
It is a textbook of self-discovery and self-awareness.

535
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:06,960
In fact, sometimes what you don't write

536
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:09,960
can be as revealing as what you have written.

537
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:12,960
A friend of mine recently shared with me the discovery

538
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:14,960
that in re-reading her journals,

539
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:16,960
she realized that everything she had written

540
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:18,960
centered around other people's lives,

541
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:20,960
their accomplishments, their failures,

542
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:22,960
their dreams, their needs.

543
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:24,960
I finally realized, she said,

544
00:24:24,960 --> 00:24:27,960
that I had spent most of my adult life

545
00:24:27,960 --> 00:24:30,960
as a mirror reflecting everybody else's existence

546
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:32,960
rather than as a human being

547
00:24:32,960 --> 00:24:34,960
living a life of my own.

548
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:37,960
In the pages of a journal,

549
00:24:37,960 --> 00:24:40,960
our innermost feelings and dreams are revealed,

550
00:24:40,960 --> 00:24:43,960
as are our strengths, our weaknesses,

551
00:24:43,960 --> 00:24:46,960
our positive attributes and our negative habits,

552
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:48,960
and our characteristics.

553
00:24:48,960 --> 00:24:50,960
If not in the words themselves,

554
00:24:50,960 --> 00:24:52,460
then at least between the

555
00:24:52,460 --> 00:24:53,960
lines of what we have written

556
00:24:53,960 --> 00:24:56,460
are the shadows of self-doubt,

557
00:24:56,460 --> 00:24:58,960
pride, envy, jealousy, and anger.

558
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:00,960
Just as actions speak louder than words,

559
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:03,460
so too will journals often say

560
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:05,960
more than what we have written.

561
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:08,960
A journal then should also

562
00:25:08,960 --> 00:25:10,960
capture your observations and reactions,

563
00:25:10,960 --> 00:25:13,960
for somewhere between what we see and what we do

564
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:15,960
will be revealed what we are.

565
00:25:16,960 --> 00:25:19,960
Capture on paper the events, the circumstances,

566
00:25:19,960 --> 00:25:21,960
and happenings of your life.

567
00:25:21,960 --> 00:25:23,460
Describe the near miss you had

568
00:25:23,460 --> 00:25:24,960
while driving to work on the freeway.

569
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:27,460
Outline your observations of people's

570
00:25:27,460 --> 00:25:29,960
behavior at the office party.

571
00:25:29,960 --> 00:25:31,960
Paint the picture of your day at the beach,

572
00:25:31,960 --> 00:25:35,960
the pounding surf, the soaring gulls, the distant sails.

573
00:25:35,960 --> 00:25:37,960
And then when you have written

574
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:39,960
about what your eyes have perceived

575
00:25:39,960 --> 00:25:43,960
and your ears have heard, go one step further

576
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:45,960
and describe your feelings,

577
00:25:45,960 --> 00:25:48,960
your emotional responses to life.

578
00:25:48,960 --> 00:25:50,960
Describe your feelings when you

579
00:25:50,960 --> 00:25:52,960
learned that John got the promotion

580
00:25:52,960 --> 00:25:54,960
that you felt was rightfully yours,

581
00:25:54,960 --> 00:25:57,460
or when you learned that Sally is

582
00:25:57,460 --> 00:25:59,960
getting married next month to your ex-husband.

583
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:01,960
Describe it all.

584
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:03,960
Don't miss any of the events of your life.

585
00:26:03,960 --> 00:26:05,960
Capture the joy of your victories as

586
00:26:05,960 --> 00:26:07,960
well as the agony of your defeats.

587
00:26:07,960 --> 00:26:10,960
And remember, it doesn't have to be

588
00:26:10,960 --> 00:26:13,960
a monumental occurrence to be worth capturing.

589
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:14,960
Truly, most human lives are full of ups and downs.

590
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:17,960
And we all know that.

591
00:26:17,960 --> 00:26:19,460
But the most important part of our

592
00:26:19,460 --> 00:26:20,960
lives consists of and evolve around minor happenings.

593
00:26:20,960 --> 00:26:23,960
So even a minor event and your response to it

594
00:26:23,960 --> 00:26:26,960
can have a major impact on how your life turns out.

595
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:28,960
You see, part of the human

596
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:30,960
experience, perhaps the most important part,

597
00:26:30,960 --> 00:26:32,960
lies in learning to translate these

598
00:26:32,960 --> 00:26:34,960
events which occur outside of us

599
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:39,960
into words and emotions within our inner worlds.

600
00:26:39,960 --> 00:26:41,960
The better we become at

601
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:43,960
describing what goes on around us,

602
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:44,460
the better we will be able

603
00:26:44,460 --> 00:26:44,960
to understand what is happening around us.

604
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:48,460
And we will be able to understand some of

605
00:26:48,460 --> 00:26:50,960
the conflicts and turmoils which take place within us.

606
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:53,960
Cause and effect always go hand in hand.

607
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:56,460
Trying to understand or deal with the

608
00:26:56,460 --> 00:26:58,960
effects without a clear picture of the cause

609
00:26:58,960 --> 00:27:01,960
is a rather hopeless situation to be in.

610
00:27:01,960 --> 00:27:05,460
Remember that all human emotions are effects which

611
00:27:05,460 --> 00:27:08,960
can be traced back to particular events or causes.

612
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:11,460
A better understanding of events will

613
00:27:11,460 --> 00:27:13,960
always give us a clearer picture

614
00:27:13,960 --> 00:27:15,960
of the effects we may be experiencing.

615
00:27:15,960 --> 00:27:18,960
Also on the subject of events and feelings,

616
00:27:18,960 --> 00:27:20,960
you will find as you begin to open

617
00:27:20,960 --> 00:27:22,960
up and really tell it like it is,

618
00:27:22,960 --> 00:27:26,960
that your journal becomes an excellent, empathetic friend.

619
00:27:26,960 --> 00:27:30,960
One who will listen to all you have to say

620
00:27:30,960 --> 00:27:34,960
about your joys, your pain, your fears, or your concerns.

621
00:27:34,960 --> 00:27:37,460
And I would strongly urge you to get these

622
00:27:37,460 --> 00:27:39,960
emotions out of your head and onto the page.

623
00:27:39,960 --> 00:27:43,960
For powerful negative emotions are diminished by writing,

624
00:27:43,960 --> 00:27:44,960
and powerful positive emotions are diminished by reading.

625
00:27:45,960 --> 00:27:48,960
And the more powerful positive emotions become explosive.

626
00:27:48,960 --> 00:27:52,960
You see, writing about your fear reduces its strength.

627
00:27:52,960 --> 00:27:56,960
And capturing your excitement magnifies its power.

628
00:27:56,960 --> 00:27:59,960
And feel free to...

629
00:27:59,960 --> 00:28:01,460
There is only one suggestion I would

630
00:28:01,460 --> 00:28:02,960
offer concerning the format of your journal,

631
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:04,960
and that is to record the

632
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:06,960
date, time, and location of each entry.

633
00:28:06,960 --> 00:28:08,960
Not only will this provide you

634
00:28:08,960 --> 00:28:10,960
with a means of measuring your progress,

635
00:28:10,960 --> 00:28:14,960
your growth trends, the different phases of your life,

636
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:16,960
and your changing attitudes,

637
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:19,960
but where and when you write

638
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:22,960
can in themselves provide interesting revelations.

639
00:28:22,960 --> 00:28:26,460
A man wrote to me several months ago to

640
00:28:26,460 --> 00:28:29,960
share such a discovery he made from his journals.

641
00:28:29,960 --> 00:28:31,460
It seems that in reviewing

642
00:28:31,460 --> 00:28:32,960
his writings of the past year,

643
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:36,960
he had noticed a definite negative pattern emerging.

644
00:28:36,960 --> 00:28:39,460
Every entry on a Wednesday afternoon

645
00:28:39,460 --> 00:28:41,960
or evening outlined thoughts of self-doubt,

646
00:28:41,960 --> 00:28:43,460
discouragement, and uncertainty about the

647
00:28:43,460 --> 00:28:44,960
direction you are heading in.

648
00:28:44,960 --> 00:28:47,960
It did not take long for him to

649
00:28:47,960 --> 00:28:50,960
track down the source of those defeating thoughts.

650
00:28:50,960 --> 00:28:53,960
Wednesday was the day when he had lunch

651
00:28:53,960 --> 00:28:56,960
with two colleagues from his former place of employment.

652
00:28:56,960 --> 00:29:00,960
To test the validity of his theory,

653
00:29:00,960 --> 00:29:03,460
he flipped back to the Wednesdays when,

654
00:29:03,460 --> 00:29:05,960
due to illness, vacations, or business matters,

655
00:29:05,960 --> 00:29:08,960
the luncheons had not taken place, and sure enough,

656
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:12,960
there were no negative entries on those particular days.

657
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:14,960
Having read the journal,

658
00:29:14,960 --> 00:29:17,960
having reached the conclusion that these luncheons were costing

659
00:29:17,960 --> 00:29:20,960
him far more than the price of the meal,

660
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:23,960
it did not take him long to

661
00:29:23,960 --> 00:29:26,960
take the necessary steps to solve the dilemma.

662
00:29:26,960 --> 00:29:29,960
Others have discovered such interesting tendencies as

663
00:29:29,960 --> 00:29:32,960
writing about personal concerns while at the office

664
00:29:32,960 --> 00:29:34,960
and business matters at home,

665
00:29:34,960 --> 00:29:37,460
or feeling particularly inspired and eager before

666
00:29:37,460 --> 00:29:39,960
leaving for the office in the morning

667
00:29:39,960 --> 00:29:44,960
and completely exhausted and enervated by 10 a.m.

668
00:29:44,960 --> 00:29:47,960
Remember, everything affects everything else.

669
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:49,960
Your environment, your associations,

670
00:29:49,960 --> 00:29:51,960
your family, your friends,

671
00:29:51,960 --> 00:29:54,960
even your occupation has an effect on you.

672
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:57,460
So, too, do the books you

673
00:29:57,460 --> 00:29:59,960
read, the television programs you watch,

674
00:29:59,960 --> 00:30:01,960
and the conversation you engage in.

675
00:30:01,960 --> 00:30:04,960
But influencers are often very subtle,

676
00:30:04,960 --> 00:30:07,460
making it difficult to detect the effect

677
00:30:07,460 --> 00:30:09,960
they are having until the damage is done.

678
00:30:09,960 --> 00:30:11,960
Like tiny little holes in a tire

679
00:30:11,960 --> 00:30:13,960
which can go undetected for hundreds of miles,

680
00:30:13,960 --> 00:30:18,960
the little pinpricks of subtle negative influences

681
00:30:18,960 --> 00:30:23,960
will eventually leave you just as deflated after a while.

682
00:30:23,960 --> 00:30:26,960
Your journal then becomes like a

683
00:30:26,960 --> 00:30:29,960
photograph album, capturing moments in your life.

684
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:32,960
The only difference is that a photograph album,

685
00:30:32,960 --> 00:30:35,460
kept for many years, reveals physical

686
00:30:35,460 --> 00:30:37,960
changes in yourself and your environment,

687
00:30:37,960 --> 00:30:40,460
while journals over a period of

688
00:30:40,460 --> 00:30:42,960
time reflect mental changes within yourself

689
00:30:42,960 --> 00:30:45,960
and about your environment.

690
00:30:45,960 --> 00:30:48,960
But perhaps the most important function your

691
00:30:48,960 --> 00:30:51,960
journal performs lies in the area of communications.

692
00:30:51,960 --> 00:30:53,960
First and foremost, your journal gives

693
00:30:53,960 --> 00:30:55,960
you a chance to talk to yourself

694
00:30:55,960 --> 00:30:59,460
and to hear what you are saying about

695
00:30:59,460 --> 00:31:02,960
your life, your future, your relationships, and your goals.

696
00:31:02,960 --> 00:31:04,460
As you begin to develop the

697
00:31:04,460 --> 00:31:05,960
habit of writing down your problems,

698
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:08,460
recording your observations, emotions,

699
00:31:08,460 --> 00:31:10,960
and reactions to life's events,

700
00:31:10,960 --> 00:31:13,960
you will undoubtedly find yourself both posing and

701
00:31:13,960 --> 00:31:16,960
responding to a whole new set of questions

702
00:31:16,960 --> 00:31:19,960
about your past, present, and future.

703
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:22,460
Why did I say that? Why does

704
00:31:22,460 --> 00:31:24,960
he always make me feel that way?

705
00:31:24,960 --> 00:31:27,460
If I follow this course, where

706
00:31:27,460 --> 00:31:29,960
will I be five years from now?

707
00:31:29,960 --> 00:31:31,960
As you begin to both

708
00:31:31,960 --> 00:31:33,960
ask and answer yourself on paper,

709
00:31:33,960 --> 00:31:36,960
you will be amazed at the

710
00:31:36,960 --> 00:31:39,960
incredible leaps in personal understanding and self-awareness

711
00:31:39,960 --> 00:31:41,960
you will experience.

712
00:31:41,960 --> 00:31:45,960
And remember, any positive change which occurs within you

713
00:31:45,960 --> 00:31:48,460
will ultimately manifest itself in

714
00:31:48,460 --> 00:31:50,960
a positive result outside of you,

715
00:31:50,960 --> 00:31:52,960
in your social or professional

716
00:31:52,960 --> 00:31:54,960
world, your attitude, your bank account,

717
00:31:54,960 --> 00:31:58,960
your habits, and even your appearance.

718
00:31:58,960 --> 00:32:01,960
We stand forever exposed to life and to

719
00:32:01,960 --> 00:32:04,960
the endless variations that make up the human drama.

720
00:32:04,960 --> 00:32:07,960
Our task as human beings is twofold.

721
00:32:07,960 --> 00:32:09,960
First, we must effectively translate

722
00:32:09,960 --> 00:32:11,960
what is going on around

723
00:32:11,960 --> 00:32:13,960
us into terms we can comprehend.

724
00:32:13,960 --> 00:32:15,960
And second, we must effectively express

725
00:32:15,960 --> 00:32:17,960
what is going on within us

726
00:32:17,960 --> 00:32:21,960
into terms the rest of the world can understand.

727
00:32:21,960 --> 00:32:24,460
Despite the major technological advances

728
00:32:24,460 --> 00:32:26,960
enabling us to communicate globally

729
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:29,960
and perhaps even extraterrestrially,

730
00:32:29,960 --> 00:32:32,460
I would suggest that while our

731
00:32:32,460 --> 00:32:34,960
means of communication has greatly improved,

732
00:32:34,960 --> 00:32:36,960
we are still living in the dark ages

733
00:32:36,960 --> 00:32:38,960
when it comes to saying what we mean,

734
00:32:38,960 --> 00:32:43,960
and understanding the meaning of what is being said.

735
00:32:43,960 --> 00:32:46,960
As William James wisely observed,

736
00:32:46,960 --> 00:32:49,960
the most immutable barrier in nature

737
00:32:49,960 --> 00:32:52,960
is between one man's thoughts and another's.

738
00:32:52,960 --> 00:32:55,960
As much as we live together, work

739
00:32:55,960 --> 00:32:58,960
together, try together, grow together, discover together,

740
00:32:58,960 --> 00:33:01,960
explore together, and even pray together,

741
00:33:01,960 --> 00:33:04,960
man is truly an island unto himself,

742
00:33:04,960 --> 00:33:06,460
cut off from other human islands

743
00:33:06,460 --> 00:33:07,960
by the deep channel of nature.

744
00:33:08,960 --> 00:33:10,960
But the world is still a place of non-communication.

745
00:33:10,960 --> 00:33:12,960
Writing in your journal is one

746
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:14,960
of the best ways I know of

747
00:33:14,960 --> 00:33:17,960
to develop more effective communication skills.

748
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:21,960
As you become better at describing life to yourself,

749
00:33:21,960 --> 00:33:24,460
you will find that you become

750
00:33:24,460 --> 00:33:26,960
better at describing yourself to life.

751
00:33:26,960 --> 00:33:28,960
Put into more practical terms,

752
00:33:28,960 --> 00:33:31,960
as you become better at saying what you really want

753
00:33:31,960 --> 00:33:34,960
and how you really feel to yourself,

754
00:33:34,960 --> 00:33:37,960
you will be able to better express yourself

755
00:33:37,960 --> 00:33:39,960
and your feelings to others,

756
00:33:39,960 --> 00:33:41,960
and in return,

757
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:44,960
better able to understand what others are really feeling

758
00:33:44,960 --> 00:33:47,960
and really saying to you.

759
00:33:47,960 --> 00:33:51,960
You see, communicating with people our own age

760
00:33:51,960 --> 00:33:54,960
or who have similar educational backgrounds,

761
00:33:54,960 --> 00:33:57,960
incomes, professions, or beliefs

762
00:33:57,960 --> 00:34:00,960
is a relatively easy process.

763
00:34:00,960 --> 00:34:02,960
But what about the two people

764
00:34:02,960 --> 00:34:04,960
who are, to all outward appearances,

765
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:06,960
radically different?

766
00:34:06,960 --> 00:34:09,960
A teenager and a 40-year-old father,

767
00:34:09,960 --> 00:34:12,960
a high school dropout and a college professor,

768
00:34:12,960 --> 00:34:16,960
a successful lawyer and an unemployed auto worker.

769
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:19,960
Now the real challenges of

770
00:34:19,960 --> 00:34:22,960
communication begin to manifest themselves.

771
00:34:22,960 --> 00:34:24,960
But they are challenges that using

772
00:34:24,960 --> 00:34:26,960
a journal can help us overcome.

773
00:34:26,960 --> 00:34:29,960
You see, regardless of the differences in our outer worlds,

774
00:34:29,960 --> 00:34:33,960
inside human beings are all basically alike.

775
00:34:33,960 --> 00:34:35,960
We've all known sorrow,

776
00:34:35,960 --> 00:34:37,960
maybe not from the same event,

777
00:34:37,960 --> 00:34:39,960
but we've all experienced the emotion.

778
00:34:39,960 --> 00:34:42,960
We've all known the joy of achievement,

779
00:34:42,960 --> 00:34:44,960
perhaps in different circumstances,

780
00:34:44,960 --> 00:34:46,960
but certainly the same feeling.

781
00:34:46,960 --> 00:34:48,960
Regardless of our outward differences,

782
00:34:48,960 --> 00:34:51,960
those basic human needs and emotions

783
00:34:51,960 --> 00:34:53,960
will always provide a common ground

784
00:34:53,960 --> 00:34:57,960
or build a bridge for effective human communications.

785
00:34:57,960 --> 00:35:00,960
You see, by the time we have reached adulthood,

786
00:35:00,960 --> 00:35:02,960
most of us have experienced almost

787
00:35:02,960 --> 00:35:04,960
every aspect of the human drama,

788
00:35:04,960 --> 00:35:06,960
in one form or another.

789
00:35:06,960 --> 00:35:09,460
The problem is that most of the

790
00:35:09,460 --> 00:35:11,960
experiences have gone right on by us.

791
00:35:11,960 --> 00:35:15,960
We have never taken the time to capture them,

792
00:35:15,960 --> 00:35:16,960
to ponder them,

793
00:35:16,960 --> 00:35:19,960
to analyze how we felt at that time,

794
00:35:19,960 --> 00:35:21,460
how we responded to others

795
00:35:21,460 --> 00:35:22,960
while we were in those circumstances,

796
00:35:22,960 --> 00:35:25,460
or what our priorities and needs

797
00:35:25,460 --> 00:35:27,960
were during that period in our lives.

798
00:35:27,960 --> 00:35:30,960
Suppose, however,

799
00:35:30,960 --> 00:35:32,460
that you took the time to capture

800
00:35:32,460 --> 00:35:33,960
the events and happenings of your life,

801
00:35:33,960 --> 00:35:36,960
on purpose, with paper and pen,

802
00:35:36,960 --> 00:35:39,460
so that you always had a

803
00:35:39,460 --> 00:35:41,960
wealth of experiences from which to draw.

804
00:35:41,960 --> 00:35:44,460
Imagine now what an incredible impact

805
00:35:44,460 --> 00:35:46,960
this awareness could have on your life,

806
00:35:46,960 --> 00:35:48,460
how it could help to bridge

807
00:35:48,460 --> 00:35:49,960
the gap between you and your children,

808
00:35:49,960 --> 00:35:53,960
your clients, your associates, your neighbors.

809
00:35:53,960 --> 00:35:55,960
You see, if you will but take the

810
00:35:55,960 --> 00:35:57,960
time to capture how it is for you

811
00:35:57,960 --> 00:36:00,960
at any given point in your life,

812
00:36:00,960 --> 00:36:02,960
then you will always be in a position to relate

813
00:36:02,960 --> 00:36:05,460
to how it might be for someone

814
00:36:05,460 --> 00:36:07,960
else at this moment in their lives.

815
00:36:07,960 --> 00:36:09,960
The situations might be different,

816
00:36:09,960 --> 00:36:12,960
but the basic needs and emotions never are.

817
